      "data": {
        "official_name": "Common Weakness Enumeration",
        "common_name": "CWE",
        "alternate_names": null,
        "description": "The canonical software and hardware weakness taxonomy, operated by MITRE.",
        "notes": "Hierarchical taxonomy with three structural levels: views (organize weaknesses by perspective, e.g., CWE-1000 Research Concepts), groupings/categories (group related weaknesses, e.g., CWE-19 Data Processing Errors; renamed from Category to Grouping in CWE 5.0 / Schema 8.0), and weaknesses (specific flaw types, e.g., CWE-79 XSS). Over 950 weakness entries (1,477 total entries in CWE 5.0: 984 weaknesses, 431 groupings/categories, 62 views). Referenced by CVE, NVD, and virtually all vulnerability databases.\n\nAI/ML weaknesses added in the CWE-1400 series: CWE-1425 (Weaknesses Related to AI/ML Products view), CWE-1426 (Improper Validation of Generative AI Output), CWE-1427 (Improper Neutralization of Input for LLM Prompting), CWE-1434 (Insecure ML Model Inference Parameters).\n\nMultiple representations: Every CWE identifier resolves to its HTML definition page on cwe.mitre.org (weight 100, text/html) as well as to its type-specific official MITRE CWE REST API JSON endpoint at https://cwe-api.mitre.org/api/v1/ (/cwe/weakness/{num}, /cwe/category/{num}, or /cwe/view/{num} at weight 50, plus universal entry-type lookup /cwe/{num} at weight 40, application/json). Filter with ?content_type=application/json to return only REST API endpoints.",
